course: dictionary
lesson: 2865
title: Dominant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dominant means the strongest, most important or most powerful in a group. Read the words around it for clues. «Real meerkats live in groups of up to about 50 in southern Africa, led by a dominant female who has most of the pups.» The group has one leader, and she has most of the pups, so dominant means the strongest one in charge.
explain: Dominant can also mean the most noticeable, the one you see most. A dominant colour in a painting is the colour that stands out most. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "the strongest one in charge" fits the meerkat sentence, so you know you have it right.
explain: Dominant is also used in science and music, where it has special meanings. You do not need to know those yet. When a word has more than one meaning, read the whole sentence, and the other words will tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Dominant means the strongest, most important or most powerful in a group.
fact: «A dominant team» is a team that is stronger than all the others.
fact: Dominant can also mean the most noticeable, like a dominant colour.
fact: In genetics, a dominant gene's feature shows up even if you got the gene from only one parent.
fact: In music, the dominant is the fifth note of a scale.
exercise: «Real meerkats live in groups of up to about 50, led by a dominant female.» What does dominant mean here? | *The strongest, most powerful one in charge | The newest arrival to the group | The smallest and quietest one | A female who lives alone
exercise: Ella says «a dominant colour» in a painting. What does it mean? | The colour nobody likes | *The colour you notice most | The colour of the paper underneath | The colour that is faded and pale
exercise: Most people have a dominant hand. What does that mean? | The hand that is always cold | The hand that is hurt | The hand they use least | *The hand they usually write with
test: «The dominant player scored three goals and led the team.» Which word means the same as dominant here? | Kind | Weak | *Strongest | Quiet
test: Which word means the most powerful in a group? | Silent | Dominant | *Dominant, meaning the strongest one in charge, is the answer here | Gentle
exam: Which sentence uses dominant correctly? | *The dominant wolf led the pack across the snow | The dominant bus was late this morning | The dominant spoon was lost in the bath | The dominant cat was sleeping on the wall in the sun
